<title>POLAND: Polisa tumbles day after bourse debut.</title>
<headline>Polisa tumbles day after bourse debut.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish insurer Polisa SA plunged the daily maximum 10 percent the day after it started trade 12.5 percent above issue, hurt by its poor fundamentals versus the other bourse insurer Warta, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;Warta simply looks better fundamentally,&quot; one trader said about the insurer whose initial public offering in late 1995 was about 37-percent subscribed.</p>
<p>Analysts said the stronger selling after price fixing signalled another possible fall for Polisa on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
